  "result": "Admins can now rename a product with `PATCH /products/:id`. `npm test` passes, 33 of 33. You don't need to do anything.\n\nAfter a rename, the new name shows here:\n- **The product itself and the product lists.** Saved copies of the old pages are cleared.\n- **Search.** The new name is found. The old name no longer finds it.\n- **Carts.**\n- **Wishlists.**\n\nPast orders keep the old name. `docs/orders.md` says order lines are never changed once an order exists.\n\nOther rules:\n- Only admins can rename.\n- A name already used by another product is refused with `409`.\n- Each rename is logged as `product.renamed`, with the old and new name.\n\nThe route is in `src/products/handlers.mjs`. I added `renameProduct` to `src/carts/store.mjs` and `src/wishlists/store.mjs`. I also added one test to `test/products.test.mjs`. Nothing is committed yet.",
